WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.280
They're more than just flickering images on
a screen,

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.580
drug public service announcements have been
a part of your life

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.440
and a part of your nightmares for decades.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:11.260
Join us as we count down 5 drug PSAs that
tried to scare the shit out of us but really didn't.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.320
Any questions?

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.060
Number 5 is 'This is Your Brain on Eggs'

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:18.780
This is drugs, this is your brain on drugs.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.860
If this late 80s ad brought to you by the
Partnership for a Drug Free America

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:22.820
didn't scare you,

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.880
maybe the follow-up containing your scary
alpha male dad did.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.900
This is your brain, this is drugs, this is
your brain on drugs.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.860
The ad was also remade about a decade later.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.040
This is your brain.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.560
Except this time with scary tank tops.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.400
And this is heroin.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.220
It's not over yet.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:44.160
This is what your family goes through, and
your friends, and your money,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.520
and your self respect and your future.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.760
Any questions?

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:49.900
Any questions?

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.039
Any questions?

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:53.729
Number 4 is doctor recommended psychedelic
cartoons.

00:00:53.729 --> 00:00:58.480
It's stimulating, it's the in thing, the hula
hoop of the jet generation.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.220
This one is from the American Medical Association
in the 1960s

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.620
and to really understand the irony of it's
message

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:06.210
you're gonna want to take a few bong rips
and turn out the lights.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:11.400
The human brain, after all, is made for thinking,
not fumigating.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.440
It's hardly a tinker toy for experimenting
with drugs.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.720
It's use can lead to abnormal behavior, to
psychological dependence

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.080
and to abuse of other drugs.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.140
Number 3, who taught you how to drug?

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.540
Answer me, who taught you how to do this stuff?

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:27.720
You alright?

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.460
I learned it by watching you.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:34.120
Parents who use drugs have children who use
drugs.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.600
There isn't much to say about this one.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.980
You already know it's stupid.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.479
People have been making parodies of the ad
for years.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.640
Who taught you how to use this thing?

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.460
You alright, I learned from watching you!

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.469
I learned it from watching you!

00:01:46.469 --> 00:01:48.620
I learned it from watching you!

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.000
Who gave you these, who taught you about these?

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.460
I learned it from you, okay?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.159
I learned it from watching you!

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.500
Number 2 is Mr T chokes the drugs out of us.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.600
Little kids doing drugs, it turns my stomach.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.119
Aw that's spilled milk Mr T.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.560
It hurts the user, it hurts his family.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.460
That's got to be like a hundred pounds of
bling there,

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.120
it's a wonder his neck doesn't fall off.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.280
It hurts his friends, I just want to shake
some sense into you kids.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.200
Mr T no!

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.540
That are using drugs or thinking about using.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.380
Mr T!

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.420
So remember don't, or else.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.460
Yeah, sorry T but your aggressive tactics
didn't stop kids from getting hooked on the junk.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.440
But let's hope another message you made did.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.440
Treat her right, treat your mother right.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.400
Treat her right, treat her right.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.600
Mother, there is no other, like mother.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.240
So treat her right.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.440
Number 1 is Peewee cracks us up.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.880
This is crack, rock cocaine.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.030
Yes Peewee Herman of Peewee's playhouse,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.240
the guy whose show felt like a dorm room acid
trip

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.360
with it's talking chairs, Genies and dinosaurs.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.580
Which begs the question, is this character
really the best pitch man for the war on drugs?

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:01.020
Everybody wants to be cool, but doing it with
crack isn't just wrong,

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.560
it could be dead wrong.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.960
So if Peewee taught us anything about drugs...

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.640
I don't know, sorry guys, I took a few puffs
while watching those Peewee's Playhouse clips.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.580
And that's 5, we hope we didn't scare you
too much.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:14.980
If you aren't high as a kite right now

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.720
post some links to more drug PSAs in the comment
section below.

